const QUESTIONS = [{"q":"You are going to a customer's home. You remember you left your glass cleaner at the office. What do you do?","opts":["Clean without it and say nothing to the customer.","Tell the customer and find a safe tool to use instead.","Use the customer's own cleaner without asking them.","Skip the glass part and hope nobody notices it."],"correct":1,"cat":"SituationHandling","scored":true,"id":0},{"q":"You break a small decoration in a room. The customer is in another room. What do you do first?","opts":["Go to the customer, say sorry, and tell them what happened.","Clean the area first and try to fix it before telling anyone.","Say nothing and hope the customer did not see.","Think the customer already knows."],"correct":0,"cat":"Honesty","scored":true,"id":1},{"q":"You see an open jewelry box on a table you need to dust. What do you do?","opts":["Close the box yourself to keep the jewelry safe.","Move the jewelry carefully and then dust the box well.","Dust around it without touching it or asking anyone.","Ask the customer if you should move it or skip it."],"correct":3,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":2},{"q":"You finish your work before the booked time ends. What is the best thing to do?","opts":["Work extra time and ask the customer for more money.","Wait in your car until the booked time is finished.","Check your work once more, then ask if they want more.","Go home right away without telling the customer or office."],"correct":2,"cat":"Time","scored":true,"id":3},{"q":"A customer shows you a small spot in the kitchen that you missed. What do you do?","opts":["Say sorry and promise to do better next time.","Say thank you and clean it right now.","Say you were following your checklist.","Say that spot was already very dirty."],"correct":1,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":4},{"q":"A customer asks you to clean balcony glass on a high floor with a tall step ladder. This is against your safety training. What do you do?","opts":["Say politely that it is not safe, and offer a safer way.","Do it the way the customer asks, to keep them happy.","Do it very fast so there is less risk.","Leave the house right away and call the office to complain."],"correct":0,"cat":"Safety","scored":true,"id":5},{"q":"A customer is angry and speaks in a loud voice about the service. What do you do?","opts":["Stay quiet and keep cleaning until they stop talking.","Leave the house at once and call the office for help.","Tell them they are wrong and defend your work.","Stay calm, listen, say sorry, and try to fix the problem."],"correct":3,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":6},{"q":"You are given many rooms in a big villa. How do you decide where to start?","opts":["Start with the room that looks the dirtiest to you.","Start with the easiest room so you finish it fast.","Ask the customer which area they want finished first.","Start with the room the customer uses the most."],"correct":2,"cat":"Time","scored":true,"id":7},{"q":"You are alone. One room is much dirtier than you thought and you are running late. What do you do?","opts":["Clean that room fast and skip the small details everywhere.","Call the office for more time and do the main areas first.","Work faster and clean less carefully in every room.","Keep your normal speed and leave the last tasks not done."],"correct":1,"cat":"Time","scored":true,"id":8},{"q":"You think the booked time is not enough to do everything well. What do you do?","opts":["Do the most important areas first and tell the office.","Work very fast and clean badly in every room.","Skip the small details in every room and hope it is okay.","Work extra time for free to be nice to the customer."],"correct":0,"cat":"Time","scored":true,"id":9},{"q":"Cleaning work often means the same tasks every day. How do you feel about this?","opts":["I get bored, so I do it faster and with less care.","I only like jobs that change every day.","I want to do it my own way, not by the steps.","That is fine. I will keep the same good work every day."],"correct":3,"cat":"Attitude","scored":true,"id":10},{"q":"Which sentence is best about training?","opts":["I follow the rules only when a supervisor is checking me.","I like to do it my own way, not like the training.","I take training seriously, even when no one is watching.","I only want to finish the work as fast as I can."],"correct":2,"cat":"Attitude","scored":true,"id":11},{"q":"Another company offers you a higher salary. What do you do first?","opts":["Leave this job right now, because the pay is higher.","Compare both jobs: pay, benefits, and how safe the job is.","Ask your customer to pay you more money to stay.","Take the new job and keep this one without telling anyone."],"correct":1,"cat":"Attitude","scored":true,"id":12},{"q":"How long do you want to work as an on-call cleaner?","opts":["For a long time, so I can build good customer trust.","Until I find a better job with higher pay somewhere.","Until I have enough experience to move to another field.","Only as long as the work place is good for me."],"correct":0,"cat":"Intent","scored":true,"id":13},{"q":"You start work at a new customer's home. What is most important?","opts":["Finish as fast as possible.","Use the smallest amount of cleaning products.","Work alone and do not ask questions.","Understand what the customer needs."],"correct":3,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":14},{"q":"You see water leaking under the kitchen sink. The customer is not home. What do you do?","opts":["Hide the leak with furniture so nobody sees it.","Try to fix the pipes yourself with your own tools.","Put a towel down and tell the customer right away.","Think the customer already knows about the leak."],"correct":2,"cat":"Honesty","scored":true,"id":15},{"q":"A customer asks you to do a job that is not in your booking. What do you do?","opts":["Do it for free to be nice to the customer.","Say it is not in the booking and offer to ask the office.","Say you do not have time and walk away quickly.","Do it, and then ask the customer for a cash tip."],"correct":1,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":16},{"q":"The customer's dog is in the room and you cannot clean safely. What do you do?","opts":["Ask the customer politely to keep the pet away while you clean.","Push the pet out of the room yourself without asking.","Wait for the pet to leave, even if the job gets late.","Skip the room and say nothing to the customer about it."],"correct":0,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":17},{"q":"Can a skilled cleaner skip some steps to save time and still get the same quality?","opts":["Yes, if you have a lot of experience.","Yes, if the customer is not looking.","Yes, if you are running late.","No. Every step is there for a reason."],"correct":3,"cat":"Attitude","scored":true,"id":18},{"q":"You make a mistake you cannot fix, like a stain on a carpet. What is best?","opts":["Say the carpet was already dirty.","Clean the rest of the house extra well so they are not angry.","Tell the customer right away and call the office for help.","Cover the stain with furniture."],"correct":2,"cat":"Honesty","scored":true,"id":19},{"q":"A customer offers to pay you in cash, outside the company, to save fees. What do you do?","opts":["Say yes. It is good for both of you, and nobody will know.","Say no politely. All work must go through the company.","Say yes but still tell the company about the booking.","Say you will think about it and talk about it later."],"correct":1,"cat":"Honesty","scored":true,"id":20},{"q":"You find a banknote on the floor while cleaning. What do you do?","opts":["Leave it where it can be seen and tell the customer.","Keep it, because it is a small amount of money.","Leave it there and say nothing about it to anyone.","Ask a coworker what to do before you decide."],"correct":0,"cat":"Honesty","scored":true,"id":21},{"q":"Nobody from the office or the customer is checking you. Does your work change?","opts":["Yes. I only clean what the customer might check.","Yes. I work faster because no one is watching.","A little. I relax because no one will know.","No. I work the same way if someone is watching or not."],"correct":3,"cat":"Attitude","scored":true,"id":22},{"q":"You find a bottle with no label at the customer's home. You do not know what it is. What do you do?","opts":["Use it because it looks like a product you know.","Mix it with your own cleaner to test it.","Ask the customer what it is, or use your own products instead.","Throw the bottle away without asking the customer first."],"correct":2,"cat":"Safety","scored":true,"id":23},{"q":"The vacuum cord is damaged and you can see the wire. What do you do?","opts":["Keep using it carefully.","Stop using it and tell the office.","Wrap it with tape and keep using it.","Use it only on dry floors."],"correct":1,"cat":"Safety","scored":true,"id":24},{"q":"You need to clean a high shelf. There is only a wobbly chair. What is the safest way?","opts":["Use a long duster or pole from the floor.","Stand on the wobbly chair and hold on to the wall.","Ask a family member to hold the chair.","Skip the shelf and say nothing to the customer."],"correct":0,"cat":"Safety","scored":true,"id":25},{"q":"A heavy piece of furniture is too hard to lift alone. The customer wants you to clean behind it. What do you do?","opts":["Lift it anyway so that you can finish the job fast.","Drag it hard across the floor to move it away.","Skip it and say nothing to the customer about it.","Ask to clean around it, or ask for help."],"correct":3,"cat":"Safety","scored":true,"id":26},{"q":"What is the safest way to use cleaning chemicals?","opts":["Mix chemicals together for a stronger clean.","Keep all chemicals together in one place.","Read the label and never mix chemicals.","Use a lot of chemical for a better result."],"correct":2,"cat":"Safety","scored":true,"id":27},{"q":"You see a loose electric socket near a wet area you need to clean. What do you do?","opts":["Clean it like normal because sockets are usually fine.","Clean around it carefully and tell the customer or office.","Try to fix the loose socket by yourself right now.","Cover the socket with a wet cloth and keep going."],"correct":1,"cat":"Safety","scored":true,"id":28},{"q":"A customer asks you to clean the outside of upper-floor windows with no safety equipment. What do you do?","opts":["Say no politely and offer to clean from inside.","Do it while holding on to the window frame tightly.","Do it quickly. It is only one time.","Ask a family member to hold your legs."],"correct":0,"cat":"Safety","scored":true,"id":29},{"q":"What is the best first safety step before you start cleaning?","opts":["Start cleaning right away so you can save time.","Ask the customer for tea and chat before you start.","Think that a home is always safe to work in.","Look around for dangers, like a wet floor or open wires."],"correct":3,"cat":"Safety","scored":true,"id":30},{"q":"You spill cleaning liquid on a tile floor and it is slippery. What do you do first?","opts":["Keep cleaning and wipe up the spill later on.","Leave it there. It will dry by itself soon.","Wipe it up now and warn people nearby.","Put a rug over the wet spot so no one sees."],"correct":2,"cat":"Safety","scored":true,"id":31},{"q":"You feel dizzy after using a strong chemical. What do you do?","opts":["Keep going and finish the job before you rest.","Stop, go to fresh air, and tell the customer and the office.","Drink water and keep using the same chemical again.","Go to another room and say nothing to anyone."],"correct":1,"cat":"Safety","scored":true,"id":32},{"q":"You break the customer's item and nobody saw it. What do you do?","opts":["Tell the customer honestly and report it to the office.","Say nothing about it, because nobody saw you.","Hide the broken pieces in your bag or the trash.","Quietly buy a new one and say nothing."],"correct":0,"cat":"Honesty","scored":true,"id":33},{"q":"A customer leaves cash on the table and says nothing. What do you do?","opts":["Take it, because it must be a tip for you.","Leave it there on the table and say nothing.","Take half of the money and leave half there.","Ask the customer first if the money is for you."],"correct":3,"cat":"Honesty","scored":true,"id":34},{"q":"You finish earlier than the booked time. What do you do?","opts":["Leave right away and tell no one that you finished early.","Stay and do nothing so it looks like full time.","Tell the customer or office the real time you finished.","Ask the customer to sign for the full booked time anyway."],"correct":2,"cat":"Honesty","scored":true,"id":35},{"q":"A coworker asks you to clock in for them. They are not at work yet. What do you do?","opts":["Do it, because it is only a small favor to a friend.","Say no and explain that you cannot do that.","Do it and ask them to do a favor for you back.","Say nothing and just walk away from your coworker."],"correct":1,"cat":"Honesty","scored":true,"id":36},{"q":"Some food or drink of the customer is missing. You did not take it. What do you do?","opts":["Tell the customer you noticed it, so you are open with them.","Say nothing and hope that they do not notice it.","Say that another cleaner must have taken it from the kitchen.","Never go to that home again after this happens."],"correct":0,"cat":"Honesty","scored":true,"id":37},{"q":"You use more of the customer's cleaning supply than normal. What do you do?","opts":["Say nothing. It is a small amount.","Add water to the bottle to hide it.","Bring your own next time and say nothing.","Tell the customer so they can buy more."],"correct":3,"cat":"Honesty","scored":true,"id":38},{"q":"A customer offers you a good review if you skip part of the cleaning list. What do you do?","opts":["Say yes. It is good for both of you.","Say yes but still do the full job.","Say no politely and do the full cleaning list.","Call the police on the customer."],"correct":2,"cat":"Honesty","scored":true,"id":39},{"q":"You find a credit card or ID card while cleaning. What do you do?","opts":["Move it somewhere you think is safer and tell no one.","Leave it where it can be seen and tell the customer.","Take a photo of it for yourself to keep.","Ignore it and keep cleaning the room as usual."],"correct":1,"cat":"Honesty","scored":true,"id":40},{"q":"Someone asks about your past work experience. What do you do?","opts":["Tell the truth about your real experience and skills.","Say you have more experience than you really have.","Say what they want to hear.","Do not answer the question."],"correct":0,"cat":"Honesty","scored":true,"id":41},{"q":"You made a mistake on a work or attendance report. What do you do?","opts":["Leave it as it is because the mistake is small.","Ask a coworker to cover for you.","Delete the whole report so no one can see it.","Fix it honestly and tell the office if needed."],"correct":3,"cat":"Honesty","scored":true,"id":42},{"q":"A customer speaks a language you do not know well. How do you understand the work to be done?","opts":["Guess what they want and start the work right away.","Do not talk to them and just clean what you see.","Use simple words or signs, and check before you start.","Do only the jobs you are sure about and skip the rest."],"correct":2,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":43},{"q":"A customer wants more rooms cleaned that are not in the booking. What do you say?","opts":["Say no and leave the house without more talking.","Explain the booking and offer to ask the office to add rooms.","Do it for free so that there is no problem.","Do it and take extra cash from the customer directly."],"correct":1,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":44},{"q":"You arrive at a new home. What is a good first step with the customer?","opts":["Check the work to be done and ask about any special wishes.","Start cleaning without speaking to the customer at all.","Ask the customer for a tip before you start work.","Wait until the customer explains every single item to you."],"correct":0,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":45},{"q":"The customer says, 'Just clean everything.' What do you do?","opts":["Guess what they mean and clean random places.","Clean only the places that look the dirtiest to you.","Skip any place that is not clear to you.","Ask a few simple questions and follow your checklist."],"correct":3,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":46},{"q":"The customer is not home and you have a question during the job. What do you do?","opts":["Guess and do what you think is best for them.","Stop working and wait until they come back home.","Call the customer, and if no answer, call the office.","Skip the unclear parts and leave when you finish."],"correct":2,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":47},{"q":"A customer likes your work and asks for your phone number to book you outside the app. What do you do?","opts":["Give your number, because it feels nice to be asked.","Say no politely. All bookings must go through the company.","Give a wrong number so they cannot call you.","Agree but ask them to keep it secret."],"correct":1,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":48},{"q":"You will be late for a booking. What do you do?","opts":["Tell the customer or office as early as you can.","Arrive late and say nothing to the customer or office.","Cancel the booking without telling the customer or office.","Send a friend in your place without telling the office."],"correct":0,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":49},{"q":"The customer is not happy but you think your work was good. What do you do?","opts":["Argue with them until they agree that you are right.","Ignore them, because you know that you did well.","Tell them to expect less next time.","Listen politely and fix what they point out."],"correct":3,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":50},{"q":"What is a good last step with the customer at the end of the job?","opts":["Leave as soon as the booked time ends, without a word.","Ask for a tip before they check the work.","Walk around with the customer and check that everything is okay.","Ask them to sign the paper quickly before they look."],"correct":2,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":51},{"q":"A customer asks about price or company rules and you do not know the answer. What do you do?","opts":["Make up an answer so that you look smart.","Say you are not sure and offer to ask the office.","Do not answer and change the topic quickly.","Tell them to find out by themselves later."],"correct":1,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":52},{"q":"You have four tasks but time for only three. How do you choose what to skip?","opts":["Choose by what the customer wants most, and tell them.","Skip the hardest one because it takes long.","Do a little of every task and finish none.","Pick one task to skip by choosing at random."],"correct":0,"cat":"Time","scored":true,"id":53},{"q":"You arrive and the home is much bigger than the booked time allows. What do you do first?","opts":["Rush through every room very quickly without any checking.","Clean only half of the home and then go.","Stay longer than booked without telling anyone at all.","Tell the customer or office, and do the main areas first."],"correct":3,"cat":"Time","scored":true,"id":54},{"q":"What is the best way to plan many bookings in one day?","opts":["Rush every job so that you have free time later.","Do the jobs in any order that you like best.","Plan real time for each job, with travel time included.","Skip the last job if you feel tired by then."],"correct":2,"cat":"Time","scored":true,"id":55},{"q":"The customer asks nicely for one small extra task that takes one minute. What do you do?","opts":["Always say no to every extra request, even small ones.","A quick favor is okay, but bigger requests go to the office.","Do every extra task for free, every time they ask.","Ask for cash from the customer to do it."],"correct":1,"cat":"Time","scored":true,"id":56},{"q":"The home needs a deep clean but you booked a regular clean. What do you do?","opts":["Do the regular clean well and offer a new booking for deep clean.","Do the deep clean and go over time without telling anyone.","Say you cannot work in that home and go away from it.","Rush the regular clean and then start the deep clean too."],"correct":0,"cat":"Time","scored":true,"id":57},{"q":"You have back-to-back bookings and there is bad traffic. What do you do?","opts":["Skip one booking and do not tell anyone why.","Drive fast and unsafe to catch up on time.","Clean badly at each stop to save some time.","Tell the office and customers as soon as you know."],"correct":3,"cat":"Time","scored":true,"id":58},{"q":"A room is very full of things. How do you start cleaning?","opts":["Skip the room because it would take too much time.","Move everything to another room without asking the customer.","Ask the customer how they want the things handled.","Throw away anything that looks like trash to you."],"correct":2,"cat":"Time","scored":true,"id":59},{"q":"You finish the checklist and have 20 minutes left. What do you do?","opts":["Leave early because the checklist is done now.","Do a last quality check, or ask if they need anything.","Sit down and wait until the time is over.","Start a job that is not in the booking, without asking."],"correct":1,"cat":"Time","scored":true,"id":60},{"q":"The customer asks you to eat with the family during a break. What do you do?","opts":["Say thank you, and say no or keep it short.","Say yes and take a long break with the family.","Ignore the invitation and do not say anything back.","Say yes and ask for extra food to take home."],"correct":0,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":61},{"q":"What is the right way to dress for a cleaning job?","opts":["Wear whatever is the most comfortable for you to work.","Wear nice formal office clothes to look important.","Wear whatever clothes the customer wants you to wear.","Follow the company uniform rules, clean and neat."],"correct":3,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":62},{"q":"A customer asks about your family and your money. What do you do?","opts":["Answer every question in detail and take your time.","Refuse to talk to the customer at all today.","Answer politely and shortly, then go back to the work.","Ask them the same personal questions about their life."],"correct":2,"cat":"Professionalism","scored":true,"id":63},{"q":"You see private papers at the customer's home while you clean. What do you do?","opts":["Read them because you are curious about the customer.","Do not touch or read them more than needed to clean.","Take photos of them to keep for yourself later.","Tidy the papers into piles without asking first."],"correct":1,"cat":"Professionalism","scored":true,"id":64},{"q":"A customer asks you to watch their child while they go out. What do you do?","opts":["Say politely that this is not part of your job.","Say yes because it is only a small favor.","Say yes if they pay you extra cash for it.","Say no in a rude way and leave the house."],"correct":0,"cat":"Professionalism","scored":true,"id":65},{"q":"You see a customer's open laptop or phone while cleaning. What do you do?","opts":["Look closer at it out of curiosity.","Tell the customer what you saw on it.","Take a photo of it for yourself.","Look away and continue your work."],"correct":3,"cat":"Professionalism","scored":true,"id":66},{"q":"You need to use the customer's bathroom during a job. What do you do?","opts":["Use it without asking.","Never use it, even if you urgently need to.","Ask the customer for permission first.","Use it only when the customer is not home, without asking."],"correct":2,"cat":"Professionalism","scored":true,"id":67},{"q":"A customer starts taking a photo or video of you for social media. They did not ask first. What do you do?","opts":["Say yes automatically, because it is their own home.","Ask them to check first. It is okay to say no.","Pose for more photos to be nice to them.","Ignore it and keep working as if nothing happened."],"correct":1,"cat":"Professionalism","scored":true,"id":68},{"q":"A customer makes you feel uncomfortable with rude or wrong behavior. What do you do?","opts":["End the talk politely and report it to the office quickly.","Stay quiet and keep working until the job ends.","Answer them with the same kind of rude comments.","Avoid that customer later and tell no one why."],"correct":0,"cat":"Professionalism","scored":true,"id":69},{"q":"What is the best way to use your phone during a job?","opts":["Use it all the time for calls and social media.","Leave it at home, even for emergencies.","Use it only when the customer is not looking.","Use it for emergencies and work only, not for personal use."],"correct":3,"cat":"Professionalism","scored":true,"id":70},{"q":"You use the wrong product on a delicate surface and it changes color. What do you do?","opts":["Cover the spot with furniture so nobody sees it.","Use more of the product to try to fix it.","Stop using it, tell the customer, and report to the office.","Say nothing and hope that no one ever sees it."],"correct":2,"cat":"Honesty","scored":true,"id":71},{"q":"You break a small decoration while dusting. No one is around. What do you do?","opts":["Throw the pieces away so no one sees them.","Keep the pieces, tell the customer, and report to the office.","Buy a similar one and put it there, saying nothing.","Move other items to hide the empty space."],"correct":1,"cat":"Honesty","scored":true,"id":72},{"q":"You forgot an important tool for the job. What is best?","opts":["Tell the customer or office and use the safest option.","Skip the jobs that need it and say nothing.","Ask the customer to buy a new tool for you.","Leave the job early without telling anyone why."],"correct":0,"cat":"Honesty","scored":true,"id":73},{"q":"You locked yourself out of a room you need to clean. What do you do?","opts":["Force the door open with a tool from your bag.","Climb in through the window to reach the room.","Leave and do not say that the room was skipped.","Tell the customer calmly and ask them for help."],"correct":3,"cat":"Honesty","scored":true,"id":74},{"q":"A customer says something is missing after your visit. You know you did not take it. What do you do?","opts":["Get angry and argue with the customer about it.","Refuse to talk about it and leave the home.","Stay calm, help fully, and tell the office right away.","Offer to pay for it to end the talk."],"correct":2,"cat":"Honesty","scored":true,"id":75},{"q":"You spill a little cleaner on a customer's rug and it leaves a mark. What do you do?","opts":["Turn the rug over so that the mark is hidden.","Blot it gently, then tell the customer and the office.","Say nothing because it is only a small mark.","Move the rug to another room so it is not seen."],"correct":1,"cat":"Honesty","scored":true,"id":76},{"q":"After leaving a job, you think you left a door or cabinet unlocked. What do you do?","opts":["Call the customer or office right away.","Ignore it. The job is done.","Wait until the next visit.","Think it is fine because no one complained."],"correct":0,"cat":"Honesty","scored":true,"id":77},{"q":"How do you do the same tasks every day for a long time?","opts":["Get careless when the tasks feel easy.","Do only the minimum that is needed each day.","Find shortcuts to finish faster, even if quality drops.","Keep the same good quality and care every time."],"correct":3,"cat":"Attitude","scored":true,"id":78},{"q":"You are asked to learn a new cleaning method or tool. What do you do?","opts":["Say no, because your own way already works well.","Learn it but keep using your old way.","Learn it and use it the way you were trained.","Learn it only if you are paid extra."],"correct":2,"cat":"Attitude","scored":true,"id":79},{"q":"What does good attendance mean in this job?","opts":["Come only when it is convenient for you that day.","Come on time daily, and tell the office early if you cannot.","Come most days and sometimes skip without telling anyone.","Attendance is not important if the work gets done later."],"correct":1,"cat":"Attitude","scored":true,"id":80},{"q":"Your supervisor tells you how to do better. What do you do?","opts":["Listen, think about it, and use it to improve.","Get angry and argue about it with your supervisor.","Ignore it. You know your work best.","Take it personally and think about quitting."],"correct":0,"cat":"Attitude","scored":true,"id":81},{"q":"A coworker is not doing their part on a shared job. What do you do?","opts":["Do all of their work and say nothing about it.","Complain about them to the customer during the job.","Work slowly too, so that it feels fair to you.","Talk to them first. Tell the office if it keeps happening."],"correct":3,"cat":"Teamwork","scored":true,"id":82},{"q":"What is the best mindset when you start a new job each day?","opts":["Work less on small jobs or jobs with low pay.","Work hard only when you are being checked.","Give every home the same care, big or small.","Do only the minimum to avoid any complaints."],"correct":2,"cat":"Attitude","scored":true,"id":83},{"q":"You have a personal problem and feel upset before a job. What do you do?","opts":["Let your bad mood show to the customer openly.","Stay calm and polite, and ask for support if you need it.","Cancel the job without telling the office or customer.","Tell the customer all about your personal problem in detail."],"correct":1,"cat":"Attitude","scored":true,"id":84},{"q":"What shows you can do well in this job for a long time?","opts":["Being consistent and honest, and building customer trust.","Doing just enough work to avoid any complaints.","Only trying to get the highest-paying customers.","Avoiding feedback so that there is no conflict at all."],"correct":0,"cat":"Attitude","scored":true,"id":85},{"q":"How do you store the cleaning chemicals you bring to a job?","opts":["Leave them open on the counter for easy use.","Mix some into one bottle to save space.","Leave them in any place where you last used them.","Keep them closed, with labels, away from children and pets."],"correct":3,"cat":"Safety","scored":true,"id":86},{"q":"Before you use a new product on the customer's furniture, what do you do?","opts":["Use it on the whole surface right away.","Ask the customer to test it for you.","Test a small hidden spot first.","Skip the furniture and clean other things."],"correct":2,"cat":"Safety","scored":true,"id":87},{"q":"Laundry is part of the job. How do you handle the customer's clothes?","opts":["Do it in the fastest way that you can.","Follow the care labels and the customer's instructions.","Wash all the clothes on the same machine setting.","Skip the laundry if it looks hard to do."],"correct":1,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":88},{"q":"You must move fragile things to clean. What is the right way?","opts":["Handle them carefully and put them back in the same place.","Move them fast so that you can save time.","Put them in a new random place after cleaning.","Do not clean around or under them at all."],"correct":0,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":89},{"q":"How do you use cloths and mop heads in different rooms, like the bathroom and kitchen?","opts":["Use the same cloth everywhere to save a lot of time.","Rinse the cloth in the toilet and use it again.","It does not matter if the cloth looks clean to you.","Use different cloths, or clean them well, so germs do not spread."],"correct":3,"cat":"SOP","scored":true,"id":90},{"q":"How do you handle trash at the end of a job?","opts":["Leave the bags anywhere.","Leave full bins even if the customer asked you to empty them.","Throw it away the way the customer wants.","Take the customer's trash without asking."],"correct":2,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":91},{"q":"You see mold or pests while cleaning. What do you do?","opts":["Ignore it, because it is not your job to fix.","Tell the customer and also tell the office.","Treat it with some random chemicals you have.","Cover the place so that no one can see it."],"correct":1,"cat":"Communication","scored":true,"id":92},{"q":"How do you clean near the customer's TV or computer?","opts":["Use a dry or slightly damp cloth. No liquid directly on it.","Spray cleaner right on the screen to clean it.","Never clean near them, even if they are dusty.","Unplug everything in the room without asking first."],"correct":0,"cat":"Safety","scored":true,"id":93},{"q":"You are not sure if a task is part of your job. What do you do?","opts":["Do it to avoid problems.","Refuse without a reason.","Ask the customer what the company rules are.","Ask the office or supervisor first."],"correct":3,"cat":"Teamwork","scored":true,"id":94},{"q":"Two cleaners clean the same big home. How do you divide the work?","opts":["The faster one does more, with no talking.","Each one does only the work they like.","Talk and divide the tasks clearly at the start.","Race each other to see who finishes first."],"correct":2,"cat":"Teamwork","scored":true,"id":95},{"q":"You do not agree with a decision from your supervisor. What do you do?","opts":["Ignore the decision and do it your own way.","Share your concern politely with the right person.","Complain to the customers about the office.","Say yes but do bad work on purpose."],"correct":1,"cat":"Teamwork","scored":true,"id":96},{"q":"You see a coworker doing something unsafe or against the rules. What do you do?","opts":["Speak to them, and tell the office if it is serious.","Ignore it because it is not really your problem.","Do the same because the other cleaners do too.","Post about it online so everyone can see."],"correct":0,"cat":"Teamwork","scored":true,"id":97},{"q":"How do you ask for a day off or say you cannot come to a booking?","opts":["Do not come and say nothing to anyone.","Ask a coworker to tell the office, without checking.","Tell the customer only, not the office.","Tell the office early, in the right way."],"correct":3,"cat":"Teamwork","scored":true,"id":98},{"q":"The office asks you to help with an urgent last-minute job. What do you do?","opts":["Always say no.","Say yes even if it means missing another job, and tell no one.","Tell them honestly if you are free or not.","Ignore the message."],"correct":2,"cat":"Teamwork","scored":true,"id":99},{"q":"You clean a wooden dining table. Which cloth is best so it does not scratch?","opts":["A rough scrubbing pad","A soft microfiber cloth","Steel wool or a metal brush","Any old dirty cloth"],"correct":1,"cat":"Skill","scored":true,"id":100},{"q":"What is the right order to clean a room?","opts":["Dust and wipe the surfaces first, then clean the floor last","Clean the floor first, then dust the surfaces","Clean only the windows and leave the rest","The order does not matter if it all gets done"],"correct":0,"cat":"SOP","scored":true,"id":101},{"q":"What is best to clean glass and mirrors without streaks?","opts":["A wet cloth with only water","A rough sponge from the kitchen sink","A cloth with a little cooking oil","A clean, dry cloth with glass cleaner"],"correct":3,"cat":"Skill","scored":true,"id":102},{"q":"When you mop, how do you keep the floor safe and help it dry well?","opts":["Leave big puddles of water on the floor","Pour extra water for a deeper clean","Wring the mop well and clean in small sections","Mop only the middle of the room"],"correct":2,"cat":"Skill","scored":true,"id":103},{"q":"Why do you want to work as a cleaner with Urban Company?","opts":["I have no other option right now, so I applied","To earn a good income in a stable and honest way","A friend told me to apply, so I came","I am not sure yet why I want this job"],"correct":1,"cat":"Intent","scored":true,"id":104},{"q":"You get free training on new cleaning tools. How do you feel?","opts":["I will go and try to learn as much as I can","I will go only if it is a must","I will skip it. I already know cleaning","I will go but not pay attention"],"correct":0,"cat":"Intent","scored":true,"id":105},{"q":"How do you feel if a supervisor says your work needs to be better?","opts":["I will feel upset and stop trying to work hard","I will ignore it and keep working my way","I will argue that my way is better","I will listen carefully and try to improve"],"correct":3,"cat":"Intent","scored":true,"id":106},{"q":"A job needs more physical effort than usual. What is your attitude?","opts":["I will do it half-heartedly","I will refuse and ask for a different job","I will do my best to finish it properly","I will complain to the customer"],"correct":2,"cat":"Intent","scored":true,"id":107},{"q":"You arrive at the customer's home. They do not open the door or answer the phone. What do you do?","opts":["Leave right away and tell no one about it","Wait a short time, call again, then tell the office","Try to go in through another door of the house","Leave and never follow up with anyone about it"],"correct":1,"cat":"SituationHandling","scored":true,"id":108},{"q":"A customer asks you to use a chemical you have never used. There are no instructions. What is safest?","opts":["Read the label or ask the customer before using it","Use it the same way as a chemical you know","Mix it with your own chemicals to test it first","Skip the task and tell nobody why you skipped it"],"correct":0,"cat":"SituationHandling","scored":true,"id":109},{"q":"What do you check before you use an electric cleaner, like a vacuum?","opts":["The color and the brand of the machine","How heavy the machine is to carry","Nothing, just plug it in and start","That the cord and plug are not damaged"],"correct":3,"cat":"Skill","scored":true,"id":110},{"q":"How do you clean a bathroom so germs do not spread?","opts":["Use the same cloth for the toilet and the sink","Start with the toilet, then use that cloth on everything","Go from the cleanest area to the dirtiest area","The order does not matter in a bathroom at all"],"correct":2,"cat":"Area","scored":true,"id":111},{"q":"You make a loud noise and it disturbs someone resting in another room. What do you do?","opts":["Ignore it and keep going with your work","Say sorry politely and be more careful","Stop working and tell no one","Blame the machine for making the noise"],"correct":1,"cat":"SituationHandling","scored":true,"id":112},{"q":"How do you greet a customer when you arrive?","opts":["Greet politely, say your name, and say why you came","Walk in without saying a greeting to the customer","Wait quietly until the customer notices you there","Greet only if the customer greets you first"],"correct":0,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":113},{"q":"You get a job farther from home than usual. What do you do?","opts":["Say no right away and do not explain why","Accept it but come whenever you like to come","Ignore the job and do not answer the office","Accept it if you can, or tell the office the problem"],"correct":3,"cat":"Intent","scored":true,"id":114},{"q":"You do not know how to remove a hard stain safely. What do you do?","opts":["Try different products one by one until one works","Ignore the stain and clean the other parts","Ask your supervisor or check your training notes first","Use the strongest chemical without checking"],"correct":2,"cat":"SituationHandling","scored":true,"id":115},{"q":"What is a good hygiene habit when you clean many homes in one day?","opts":["Use the same gloves and cloths at every home","Wash your hands and use clean tools between homes","Hygiene does not matter between homes","Wash your hands only at the end of the day"],"correct":1,"cat":"Skill","scored":true,"id":116},{"q":"You feel tired in the middle of a job. What do you do?","opts":["Take a short rest if needed, then keep the same quality","Rush the rest of the job and clean carelessly","Stop the job in the middle and leave the home","Ask the customer to finish the cleaning for you"],"correct":0,"cat":"Intent","scored":true,"id":117},{"q":"How willing are you to follow the company cleaning checklist, even if it is different from your way at home?","opts":["Only if it is easier for me than my own way","I always prefer to do it my own way at work","Only when someone is watching me at work","Very willing. I will follow the training and the checklist"],"correct":3,"cat":"Intent","scored":true,"id":118},{"q":"A coworker does not follow good hygiene, and the customer may lose trust. What do you do?","opts":["Ignore it, because it is not really your job","Tell the customer about the habits of your coworker","Tell them politely, and tell the office if it continues","Do the same thing as them so it is fair"],"correct":2,"cat":"SituationHandling","scored":true,"id":119},{"q":"A house is very dirty. You have 2 hours, but a job like this usually takes 4. What do you do?","opts":["Skip the slow areas and clean only the easy ones","Find what matters most to the customer and clean those first","Clean everything at the same speed and see how far you get","Call the customer and ask for more time before you start"],"correct":1,"cat":"Time","scored":true,"id":120},{"q":"You mopped, but the floor still looks dull. What is the most likely reason?","opts":["The cleaner is wrong for that floor, or it leaves a film","The cleaner needs more time to dry before it shines","The floor is old and can never look clean","You must mop two or three more times with the same cleaner"],"correct":0,"cat":"Skill","scored":true,"id":121},{"q":"A home has a marble floor and a wooden floor. What is safest?","opts":["Use the same strong cleaner on both of the floors at home","Use a strong acid cleaner on the marble to make it shine","Only dust both floors and never use any liquid on them","Use a mild cleaner on marble and a barely damp mop on wood"],"correct":3,"cat":"Area","scored":true,"id":122},{"q":"You must disinfect the kitchen counter, but your product says 'cleaner,' not 'disinfectant.' What do you do?","opts":["Use it anyway. Cleaning and disinfecting are the same thing","Use double the amount so it works stronger on germs","It may not kill germs. Look for a disinfectant or ask what to use","Skip disinfecting today because you have no exact product"],"correct":2,"cat":"SOP","scored":true,"id":123},{"q":"You smell strong drain cleaner in the bathroom before you start. What do you do first?","opts":["Start cleaning right away with your usual products","Open a window or door first, and do not mix chemicals","Add your bleach cleaner to cover the bad smell","Ignore the smell because it will go away soon"],"correct":1,"cat":"Safety","scored":true,"id":124},{"q":"A customer asks you to clean a high chandelier and there is no stable ladder. What do you do?","opts":["Skip it, explain it is not safe, and suggest another way","Stand on the dining table or a chair to reach it","Use a long broom to knock the dust off from below","Ask the customer to hold the chair while you climb"],"correct":0,"cat":"Safety","scored":true,"id":125},{"q":"You finish the living room with 10 minutes left. Everything looks done. What do you do?","opts":["Sit down and wait for the time to end","Start a task the customer did not ask for","Leave early because the work looks done","Walk around and check corners, surfaces, and small details"],"correct":3,"cat":"Time","scored":true,"id":126},{"q":"What is the right order to clean a room, from top to bottom?","opts":["Mop the floor first, then dust the shelves, then wipe the windows","Vacuum first, then dust, so the dust falls on the clean floor","Dust high places first, then wipe surfaces, then do the floor last","The order does not matter if everything is done in the end"],"correct":2,"cat":"SOP","scored":true,"id":127},{"q":"You spill a little cleaning product on a customer's rug. What do you do first?","opts":["Rub it hard and fast with a dry kitchen cloth","Blot it gently with a clean, damp cloth. Do not rub","Leave it to dry and fix it at the end","Pour a lot of water all over the rug to wash it"],"correct":1,"cat":"Skill","scored":true,"id":128},{"q":"The customer says use only their products, but their kitchen cleaner is empty. What do you do?","opts":["Tell the customer it is empty and ask what to do","Use your own product and say nothing to the customer","Skip the kitchen and clean the other rooms only","Use only water in the kitchen without asking anyone"],"correct":0,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":129},{"q":"Which two chemicals must you never mix?","opts":["Water and dish soap together","Vinegar and plain water","Baking soda and plain water","Bleach and ammonia cleaners"],"correct":3,"cat":"Skill","scored":true,"id":130},{"q":"You clean a home with a newborn baby. What is most important?","opts":["Use the strongest chemicals so all germs are killed","Skip the baby's room and clean the other rooms","Use milder products, keep chemicals closed, and open windows","Spray a lot of air freshener in every room"],"correct":2,"cat":"Safety","scored":true,"id":131},{"q":"Your vacuum loses suction and sounds strained. What do you do?","opts":["Push it harder because it will still work in the end","Stop and check if the bag is full or something is stuck","Ignore the sound because vacuums are always noisy","Turn it off, skip the vacuuming, and tell no one"],"correct":1,"cat":"Skill","scored":true,"id":132},{"q":"A customer's rug says 'dry clean only,' and you only have wet tools. What do you do?","opts":["Skip the rug and tell the customer or supervisor","Use your wet tools carefully on the rug anyway","Use a lot of water so that it cleans well","Dry it quickly with a hair dryer after cleaning"],"correct":0,"cat":"Skill","scored":true,"id":133},{"q":"You forgot one of your cleaning tools. What do you do first?","opts":["Skip that part and say nothing to the customer","Use any product under the customer's sink without checking","Rush the task without the tool and hope no one notices","Look for a safe substitute, or tell the customer or supervisor"],"correct":3,"cat":"SituationHandling","scored":true,"id":134},{"q":"You will live in company housing with other cleaners in Saudi Arabia, away from your family. Which mindset helps you most?","opts":["Expect it to be the same as living at home with family","Complain often to the company until the housing changes","Accept shared housing as part of this job and respect others","Avoid your housemates and see it as a short problem"],"correct":2,"cat":"Lifestyle","scored":true,"id":135},{"q":"You get one day off every week, even in busy times. You feel you need one more day off. What do you do?","opts":["Do not come on a day that you choose","Ask politely, and accept the rule if it cannot change","Ask other cleaners to take an extra day off with you","Take the extra day first and explain the reason later"],"correct":1,"cat":"Lifestyle","scored":true,"id":136},{"q":"Some days have few bookings and you wait in the van. What is the best attitude?","opts":["Stay ready, because a new booking can come anytime","Think it is wasted time and ask to go home","Complain to the other cleaners about how unfair it is","Look for other jobs on your phone while you wait"],"correct":0,"cat":"Lifestyle","scored":true,"id":137},{"q":"Customers rate your work, and ratings affect your incentives. You get a lower rating than you hoped. What do you do?","opts":["Say the rating system is unfair and should end","Ignore it because one rating is not important","Stop working extra hard because you cannot control ratings","Think about what went wrong and improve next time"],"correct":3,"cat":"Lifestyle","scored":true,"id":138},{"q":"You serve many customers, some nice and some difficult. Which attitude is best?","opts":["Do your best only for polite customers","Answer rude customers in the same tone","Stay professional and do your best for every customer","Ask to leave any customer who seems difficult"],"correct":2,"cat":"Lifestyle","scored":true,"id":139},{"q":"Bookings can be 2 hours or 4 hours. You do not know which is next. How does this change how you plan?","opts":["It does not matter. Clean at the same speed always","Check the size of the work against the time","Always think it is 4 hours and work slowly","Ask the customer to make the job smaller for you"],"correct":1,"cat":"Time","scored":true,"id":140},{"q":"With travel, your work day can be 13 to 14 hours, and about 8 hours are cleaning inside homes. What does this tell you?","opts":["You need a strong body and mind for a long day","Most of the day you will have nothing to do","The extra hours are a mistake and must be reported","You will finish before 8 hours on most days"],"correct":0,"cat":"Lifestyle","scored":true,"id":141},{"q":"In the 5-day training in Saudi Arabia, trainers will push you to learn fast and follow the exact cleaning steps. How do you approach it?","opts":["Expect it to be easy because it is only training","Push back on the parts that feel too hard for you","Do it your own way if you already have experience","Take it seriously, follow instructions, and build good habits"],"correct":3,"cat":"Lifestyle","scored":true,"id":142},{"q":"Training focuses on the company's exact cleaning steps (SOP), not your own way, even if your way also cleans the house. Why does the company do this?","opts":["The company does not trust any cleaner to think","Your own way is always wrong and never works","A tested process keeps quality the same for every customer","SOP is only for people with no experience at all"],"correct":2,"cat":"Lifestyle","scored":true,"id":143},{"q":"Your first 10 customer ratings must average above 4.7 out of 5. If not, you get retraining first. How should you see this rule?","opts":["Unfair, because it does not count honest effort and hard work","A clear and fair rule, with real help before any final decision","Something to worry about only if it really happens to you","A reason to do the minimum until the first 10 ratings are done"],"correct":1,"cat":"Lifestyle","scored":true,"id":144},{"q":"Your supervisor asks you to redo part of a job because it was not good enough. What do you do?","opts":["Redo it well without excuses, and ask what to improve","Give reasons it was hard and ask them to accept it","Redo it, then complain about it to other cleaners","Do only the minimum extra to avoid more comments"],"correct":0,"cat":"Lifestyle","scored":true,"id":145},{"q":"The company changes one of its cleaning steps. What is the best reaction?","opts":["Keep using the old way because it worked fine","Use the new way only when a supervisor is watching","Ask the company to keep the old way for you","Learn the new step and use it as normal work"],"correct":3,"cat":"Lifestyle","scored":true,"id":146},{"q":"In training, a trainer corrects you in front of other trainees. What is the best reaction?","opts":["Feel shy and try less for the rest of training","Argue with the trainer that your way was fine","Accept it politely and use it. That is what training is for","Stay away from that trainer for the whole training"],"correct":2,"cat":"Lifestyle","scored":true,"id":147},{"q":"Some cleaners you know refuse certain bookings to pressure the company. What do you do?","opts":["Join them, because it is safer to stay with the group","Keep working professionally, and share concerns the right way","Refuse some bookings quietly on your own, and tell no one","Support them in public but keep working"],"correct":1,"cat":"Lifestyle","scored":true,"id":148},{"q":"You are a little late and the next customer is waiting. The customer asks for one more small task. What do you do?","opts":["Check if you can fit it in. If not, tell them honestly","Ignore the request","Do it even if the next customer has to wait a long time","Say you are too busy and end the booking"],"correct":0,"cat":"Time","scored":true,"id":149},{"q":"You left a customer's back door unlocked and you remember on the way to the next job. What do you do?","opts":["Go to the next job because you are already late for it","Tell them at the end of your shift when you finish","Say nothing unless someone asks you about the door","Call the customer or supervisor right away, even if awkward"],"correct":3,"cat":"SituationHandling","scored":true,"id":150},{"q":"Two customers on the same day make the same complaint about one area. What does this probably mean?","opts":["Both customers are just very hard to please","It is only luck and it means nothing at all","You may have a gap in how you clean that area","The two customers are working together to complain"],"correct":2,"cat":"SituationHandling","scored":true,"id":151},{"q":"A customer's pet knocks over your bucket and dirty water spills on the floor. What do you do first?","opts":["Blame the pet and wait for the customer to clean","Clean it up now and calmly tell the customer what happened","Ignore it, because it was not your fault at all","Mop it up quietly and say nothing to the customer"],"correct":1,"cat":"SituationHandling","scored":true,"id":152},{"q":"You skipped a step earlier to save time and the customer did not notice. What do you do?","opts":["Go back and finish the step properly before you leave","Say nothing, because the customer did not complain about it","Fix it only if the customer complains about it later","Tell the customer but do not fix it"],"correct":0,"cat":"SituationHandling","scored":true,"id":153},{"q":"The customer is not home and left no notes. You see dirty dishes in the sink and dust everywhere. What do you decide first?","opts":["Start with the room that feels the easiest to you","Do the least work and then call it done","Wait outside until the customer comes back home","Start with the dishes, because they affect health"],"correct":3,"cat":"Area","scored":true,"id":154},{"q":"After leaving, you think you used a weaker product on a stain the customer asked about. What do you do?","opts":["Say nothing and hope it looks fine when dry","Wait to see if the customer complains about the stain","Tell the customer or supervisor so it can be fixed","Blame the product label because it was not clear to you"],"correct":2,"cat":"SituationHandling","scored":true,"id":155},{"q":"A new cleaner asks you to cover part of their booking so they can leave early. The supervisor does not know. What do you do?","opts":["Agree quietly, because it is only a personal favor","Say no without approval, and tell them to ask properly","Agree only if they promise to give a favor back later","Report them without giving them a chance to fix it"],"correct":1,"cat":"SituationHandling","scored":true,"id":156},{"q":"The customer looks upset or stressed when you arrive, but says nothing. What do you do?","opts":["Work calmly and politely, and give them some space","Ask again and again what is wrong with them","Think it is about your work and say sorry first","Leave early because the home feels uncomfortable to you"],"correct":0,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":157},{"q":"What is the best way to clean a kitchen stove top?","opts":["Pour cold water on it while it is still hot","Wipe it with a dry cloth only and nothing else","Scrub it with steel wool on every kind of stove","Let it cool, remove food bits, then wipe with a degreaser"],"correct":3,"cat":"Area","scored":true,"id":158},{"q":"What is the right order to clean a kitchen?","opts":["Mop the floor first, then clean the counters","Clean the sink first, then the floor, then the stove","Counters and stove first, then the sink, then the floor last","The order does not matter in a kitchen"],"correct":2,"cat":"Area","scored":true,"id":159},{"q":"How do you clean the inside of a fridge?","opts":["Spray a strong cleaner right over the food inside","Take out the food, wipe the shelves with mild soapy water","Wipe only the outside door and leave the inside","Pour hot water inside the fridge to clean it"],"correct":1,"cat":"Area","scored":true,"id":160},{"q":"What is the right way to clean a toilet?","opts":["Use a brush and cleaner inside, and a separate cloth outside","Use the same cloth that you use for the sink and tap","Use the toilet brush on the bathroom floor too, to save time","Wipe the toilet seat with a cloth from the kitchen"],"correct":0,"cat":"Area","scored":true,"id":161},{"q":"How do you clean a shower glass wall without scratching it?","opts":["Use a rough scrubbing pad to remove all marks","Use steel wool on the hard spots and stains","Leave it wet so that it can dry by itself","Use a soft cloth or sponge with a mild cleaner, then dry it"],"correct":3,"cat":"Area","scored":true,"id":162},{"q":"How do you clean a bedroom the right way?","opts":["Vacuum first, and then dust the shelves after","Dust only the things you can see easily","Fix the bed, dust from top to bottom, then vacuum last","Clean only the floor and leave the other things"],"correct":2,"cat":"Area","scored":true,"id":163},{"q":"How do you clean a dusty ceiling fan?","opts":["Clean it while it is spinning to save time","Turn it off, then wipe each blade with a damp cloth","Shake the dust off into the room to clear it","Spray water on the motor to wash it clean"],"correct":1,"cat":"Area","scored":true,"id":164},{"q":"How do you clean door handles and light switches?","opts":["Wipe them with a clean cloth and a little disinfectant","Skip them because they are very small things","Spray a lot of water on the light switch","Wipe them with the same cloth as the toilet"],"correct":0,"cat":"Area","scored":true,"id":165},{"q":"What should you do before you leave the customer's home?","opts":["Leave right after you finish the last room","Leave your tools there to use the next time","Tell the customer you are done only if they ask","Check every room, take your tools, and tell the customer"],"correct":3,"cat":"SOP","scored":true,"id":166},{"q":"What is the first step when you start any cleaning job?","opts":["Start cleaning at once so that you save time","Ask the customer to leave the house for you","Greet the customer, check the work, and look for dangers","Take photos of the customer's things in the house"],"correct":2,"cat":"SOP","scored":true,"id":167},{"q":"Why do you wear gloves while cleaning?","opts":["Only to look more professional in front of customers","To protect your hands from chemicals and germs","So the customer cannot see your hands","Gloves are not needed for any job"],"correct":1,"cat":"SOP","scored":true,"id":168},{"q":"How do you use a spray bottle of cleaner on a surface?","opts":["Spray a little, wait a moment, then wipe it clean","Spray a lot so it is very wet and leave it","Spray it into the air around the room","Spray it and leave it without wiping it off"],"correct":0,"cat":"SOP","scored":true,"id":169},{"q":"Why do you follow the same cleaning steps in every home?","opts":["So that you do not have to think at work","Only because the supervisor is watching you work","There is no real reason for doing it","So quality is the same and work is faster and safer"],"correct":3,"cat":"SOP","scored":true,"id":170},{"q":"The customer asks you to use their own mop, but it is very dirty. What do you do?","opts":["Use it without saying anything to the customer","Refuse to clean the floor in that home","Tell the customer politely and ask to use your own mop","Throw the dirty mop away without asking the customer"],"correct":2,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":171},{"q":"A customer follows you around and watches everything you do. What do you do?","opts":["Tell them to stop watching you while you work","Stay calm and polite. It is okay for them to watch","Stop working until they leave the room or house","Work faster and less carefully to finish early"],"correct":1,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":172},{"q":"You have a 2-hour booking for a home with a kitchen, bathroom, and bedroom. How do you plan your time?","opts":["Plan time for each area, and start with kitchen and bathroom","Spend most of the time on the first room you see","Do not plan, just start cleaning the first thing you see","Clean the bedroom first and rush all the rest"],"correct":0,"cat":"Time","scored":true,"id":173},{"q":"A customer says the price is too high for the work you did. What do you do?","opts":["Lower the price yourself to make the customer feel happy","Argue with them that the price is fair and right","Tell them they can pay whatever amount they like","Listen politely and say the office can help with price questions"],"correct":3,"cat":"Customer","scored":true,"id":174},{"q":"How do you clean a fabric sofa?","opts":["Pour a lot of water on it to wash it","Scrub it hard with a rough brush to remove marks","Vacuum it first, then clean marks as the label says","Use strong bleach on the whole sofa to kill germs"],"correct":2,"cat":"Area","scored":true,"id":175},{"q":"Why do you use a different color cloth for the toilet and the kitchen?","opts":["To make the cleaning work look nice and colorful","To stop germs from spreading from the toilet to the kitchen","Because the colored cloths are cheaper to buy","There is no real reason for using different colors"],"correct":1,"cat":"SOP","scored":true,"id":176}];

